@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Two simultaneous PATCH requests, last write wins
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (state and API client)" #E0F2FE
  participant "HttpTodoApi request A" as a
  participant "HttpTodoApi request B" as b
end box
box "Backend — Laravel API (HTTP layer)" #D1FADF
  participant "TodoController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend — Laravel Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "UpdateTodo" as action
end box
box "Backend — Laravel Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  participant "EloquentTodoRepository" as repo
  database "MySQL database" as db
end box
a -> ctrl : PATCH /api/v1/todos/{id} with body A
b -> ctrl : PATCH /api/v1/todos/{id} with body B at the same time
ctrl -> action : handle() for A and for B
action -> repo : update(todo, changes) for A and for B
repo -> db : A sends one UPDATE statement for its changed columns and updated_at
repo -> db : B sends one UPDATE statement for its changed columns and updated_at
note right of db : InnoDB row lock serialises the two statements (L2-043 criterion 2)
db --> repo : A applied in full
db --> repo : B applied in full after A
repo --> action : Updated Todo for A and for B
action --> ctrl : Updated Todo for A and for B
ctrl --> a : 200 with the todo as saved by A
ctrl --> b : 200 with the todo as saved by B
note over db : Same field: final value equals one of the two requests. Disjoint fields: both changes present. Never a partial row (L2-043 criterion 2)
@enduml
